OL,3,GNEWSAWeed-choked river cleared allowing
OL,4,Aboats to pass
OL,5,
OL,6,FWeed has been removed from a river in
OL,7,FLincolnshire after people complained
OL,8,Fthey were unable to use the waterway.
OL,10,FAnthony Grunwell, of Spalding Water
OL,11,FTaxi and Boat Hire, said the River
OL,12,FWelland at Spalding had become
OL,13,Funnavigable, forcing him to suspend the
OL,14,Fservice for two weeks.
OL,16,FGrunwell said contractors on behalf of
OL,17,Fthe Environment Agency (EA) had started
OL,18,Fworking on Friday to lift the weed and
OL,19,Fhave done a "marvellous" job. He hopes
OL,20,Fto restart the taxi service next week.
OL,23,APub: 12-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
